WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.027
When reading recursion, identify the anchor first.

00:00:03.027 --> 00:00:09.442
Then identify the self-reference. The join condition defines how one level connects to the next.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:14.902
Adding a depth or path column can make the traversal much easier to inspect and debug.

00:00:14.902 --> 00:00:18.717
Do not try to understand the whole recursive statement at once.

00:00:18.717 --> 00:00:25.007
Recursive CTEs are useful when rows refer to other rows in a hierarchy or graph-like chain.

00:00:25.007 --> 00:00:30.387
The anchor establishes the starting set; the recursive term finds the next level.

00:00:30.387 --> 00:00:33.342
Always think about termination and cycles.

00:00:33.342 --> 00:00:37.966
Production hierarchies often need safeguards against malformed relationships.
